Just completed my third ascension. I had decided to completely random
gen a character and surprised I did pretty well--got a dwarven valk,
and while I know they're theoretically easy, I tend to get my melee-
heavy characters killed quickly from charging into battle too soon.
("But I have zillions of hit points! Surely, I will survive thi-"). I
also like and often rely on spellcasting so it was interesting playing
a character who did not have that as a reasonable option.

My chances to be careless increased when I found an aligned altar on
level 3 and got Mjollnir fairly early. But I guess knowing that I
could easily get overconfident, I just tried to hold myself back as
much I could.

After Mojo, I didn't get much magical equipment for awhile--a good
cloak of protection (not the one you see listed below) and a ring of
slow digestion were definitely helpful, but that was about it. Went
through the whole gnomish mines (slowly) with some enchanted dwarven
mithril and the like.

Sokoban yielded a bag of holding--the second one I found. I had no
reflection until Medusa when I got Perseus's shield.

I went down to the Castle and dealt with the monsters there with the
aid of a ring of conflict, and got the wand of wishing, where I got
myself (after charging, etc.) some gray dragon scale mail (magic
protection at last!) and fireproof boots of water walking so I could
deal with Lord Surtur's realm, then went back up and did the Quest.
Then it was down into the Maze, where I spent approximately six years
looking for the stairs to Vlad's Tower.

A moment of silence for my beloved pet Sally. I tamed her as a kitten
in the gnomish mines, and she grew quickly into a deadly large cat who
devoured many of my foes. Later, a polymorph trap transformed her into
a Hill Giant, whom, equipped with Ogresmasher, continued to watch my
back all the way from the early game well into Gehennom, where she
finally met her demise. Had no other pets, save briefly a black dragon
and pair of baluchitheria  who the Wizard of Yendor had summoned to
fight me; I tamed them with a scroll of taming, and he punished them
for betraying him.

Endgame was frustrating. First, I realized my Bell had gotten cursed,
and--the RNG deciding not to give me very many potions of water/areas
where I could dilute other potions--I went through a fair amount of
rigamarole to get the thing uncursed (I think finally I used my last
spare wish to get some scrolls of charging to re-charge a magic marker
and write a scroll of remove curse.... could've just wished for a
scroll of remove curse, I guess, but I was hoping to use the magic
marker charges for other things--like also make some scrolls of
enchant armor, which were also rare in the game).

I am finding I *hate* re-climbing out of Gehennom after gaining the
amulet--the random teleport downwards adds more frustration than
actual enjoyable gameplay challenge. I couldn't seem to get above
Juiblex's level to save my life, then found a cursed potion of gain
level and got up there that way. On the upside, once I got back into
the Dungeons of Doom, Rodney left me alone for the most part.

Elemental planes weren't too bad, except I realized I'd forgotten to
wish for and didn't other wise find an amulet of magical breathing, so
spent a long time in the Water Plane clinging desperately to my air
bubble until I finally got over to the portal.

Astral Plane started dodgily--I showed up, and the Angel of Tyr said
something about Conflict and started attacking me--I guess my wearing
a ring of conflict upon arrival was a bad idea. But the ring of
conflict also had a yellow dragon taking him down with some acid
breath--while in the meantime I got attacked by Death. Fortunately
killed him before he killed me and wandered right--and behold, first
altar room I get to is mine!

